---
// "Made for window cleaning": what the generic tools don't do, a plain list with no icons.
// Every line is checked against the app (decision 0044).
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="made-for-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="made-for-heading">Made for window cleaning</h2>
    <ul class="list measure">
      <li>
        Price per pane from your price book, with surcharges you name yourself, like Ladder or Roof.
        More than one can go on the same line.
      </li>
      <li>
        Runs: shops along a street done together, in the stop order you set. Each stop comes every
        run, every 2nd run or every 3rd run.
      </li>
      <li>
        Weekly, fortnightly, every 4 weeks, every so many weeks, or monthly (on a date or on a
        weekday), up to every 24 months.
      </li>
      <li>
        For customers who like to be asked first, a "due for a clean" email that you check and send.
        They tap "Book it" or "Not this time".
      </li>
      <li>The job card shows the property's access, parking and hazard notes.</li>
      <li>
        A glass scratch acknowledgement your customer signs by typing their name. The job card shows
        whether it's signed.
      </li>
      <li>
        While you're not registered for GST, invoices are headed "Invoice" with no GST line.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
